# This package intentionally carries two React majors as devDependencies (react/react-dom
# 18.3.1, plus react19/react-dom19 aliased to npm:react@19.2.0 / npm:react-dom@19.2.0) so it
# can run its own test contract against both peer-declared majors. npm's strict peer
# resolution has no way to know the aliased 19.x copies satisfy each other's internal peer
# dependency on "react" rather than the top-level 18.3.1 copy, and errors out on that
# apparent conflict. legacy-peer-deps lets npm install proceed; scripts/link-react19.mjs
# (run on postinstall) then nests each aliased package into the other's node_modules so
# plain Node resolution — not npm's peer graph — picks the matching major at runtime.
legacy-peer-deps=true
